{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1230"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge history/modern-history","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/history__modern-history.g1.json","changes":[{"field":"titleEn","old":"Five Dates That Changed the World","new":"Six Dates That Changed the World"},{"field":"titleDe","old":"Fünf Daten, die die Welt veränderten","new":"Sechs Daten, die die Welt veränderten"},{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",40],["-","five"],["+","six"],["=",29],["-","Tuesday"],["+","summer"],["=",1],["+","day "],["=",390],["+","6 June 1944 – D-Day. In the early hours of a Tuesday, after a 24-hour postponement because of storms, more than 150,000 American, British, Canadian and other Allied soldiers landed on five beaches in Normandy, code-named Utah, Omaha, Gold, Juno and Sword, supported by some 7,000 ships and landing craft and thousands of aircraft. Operation Overlord opened the long-awaited second front in the west; less than a year later Nazi Germany surrendered.\n\n"],["=",242],["-","Crowds"],["+","That"],["=",1],["+","Thursday evening crowds "],["=",234],["+","6 June 1944 | D-Day, the Allied landings | Normandy |\n| "],["=",54],["-","Five"],["+","Six"],["=",3],["-","five"],["+","six"],["=",1],["-","cities,"],["+","places,"],["=",24]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",42],["-","fünf"],["+","sechs"],["=",27],["-","Dienstag"],["+","Sommertag"],["=",379],["+","6. Juni 1944 – Der D-Day. In den frühen Morgenstunden eines Dienstags landeten nach einer sturmbedingten Verschiebung um 24 Stunden mehr als 150.000 amerikanische, britische, kanadische und weitere alliierte Soldaten an fünf Stränden der Normandie mit den Decknamen Utah, Omaha, Gold, Juno und Sword, unterstützt von rund 7.000 Schiffen und Landungsbooten und Tausenden Flugzeugen. Die Operation Overlord eröffnete die lang erwartete zweite Front im Westen; weniger als ein Jahr später kapitulierte das nationalsozialistische Deutschland.\n\n"],["=",228],["-","den"],["+","jenem"],["=",1],["-","Grenzübergängen"],["+","Donnerstagabend"],["=",5],["+","an den Grenzübergängen "],["=",218],["+","6. Juni 1944 | D-Day, die Landung der Alliierten | Normandie |\n| "],["=",50],["-","Fünf"],["+","Sechs"],["=",3],["-","fünf"],["+","sechs"],["=",1],["-","Städte,"],["+","Orte,"],["=",22]]}]},
